  "notes": [
    "Panel A uses all 910 forward technical records per signal, including observation insufficiency; these are not all global heat events or confirmed heat failures.",
    "Panel B uses complete observed integral windows without flagged interference (AP 466/129 countries; BGP 601/137; Telescope 302/93). Medians [25th, 75th percentiles] describe selected events; no heat-versus-control contrast is implied. A ratio shortfall is not a fraction of people disconnected.",
    "Panel C conditions on observed damaged-at-end cores. Unlike Panel A classification, it does not require complete subsequent observation; it can therefore contain more damaged cores than Panel A. First missing/flagged follow-up censors. Telescope has one eligible zero-follow-up record excluded from positive-time fits. Administrative and missingness censoring are not known 72-hour non-recovery.",
    "AP recovery is sparse and exploratory; BGP has no confirmed endpoints and no fitted recovery effect. Confirmation requires 24 consecutive ten-minute slots at or above 95%. These panels are distinct denominators and must not be added together."
